      "Dhanvantari is the physician of the gods and an avatar of Vishnu in the Puranic lists. The Bhagavata Purana and the Vishnu Purana tell that he arose from the Samudra Manthan, the churning of the milk ocean, carrying a pot of amrita. His four hands hold the conch, the discus, a leech and the pot of nectar in the conventional image, and his complexion is dark. The original Dhanvantari is connected with the Sushruta Samhita, which opens with the sage Sushruta hearing the science of surgery from the king of Kashi, Divodasa, in his Dhanvantari incarnation.",
